{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790716926,"nonce":"APrKj3xqb10IGssZCmjIv7OQqHU=","title":"Evaluate Std.isOfType variable targets at runtime","message":"`Std.isOfType(value, typeVariable)` desugared every call to a HIR TypeCheck using the second argument's static type. For a `Dynamic` variable holding `Int`, the compiler checked against `Dynamic` instead of `Int`. An `Array\u003cDynamic\u003e` target added a second mismatch because primitive type tokens can be held in ordinary integer boxes.\n\n`haxe-conformance/regressions/DynamicIsOfType.hx` reproduced the first failure as `Int target`. The fix preserves the static path for named type literals, carries other target expressions through HIR, and resolves raw or boxed runtime type tokens before the type check. The regression covers primitive, String, Array, null, and class hierarchy cases. All 82 authored regressions pass. In the full tiered suite, Issue4285 and Issue4962 moved from wrong answer to pass, with no status regressions. The run scored 768/1094; the unrelated Issue10083 map-order case is nondeterministic and was wrong answer in both compared runs.","files":null}]}